WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:28.041
"Wow!" said Maggie. "Look at how many people are at the horse show.

2
00:00:28.042 --> 00:00:30.917
We're going to make tons of money!"

3
00:00:30.918 --> 00:00:33.407
Henry laughed.

4
00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:38.902
"Stop counting your future profits and help me hang up our sign."

5
00:00:38.903 --> 00:00:45.603
"Sorry." Maggie held the sign while Henry tacked it to a tree near where they'd set up their lemonade stand.

6
00:00:45.604 --> 00:00:52.645
Once the sign was hung, Henry wiped his brow. "Wow, it's pretty hot today."

7
00:00:52.646 --> 00:00:58.393
"I know." Maggie smiled. "That should make people buy even more lemonade.

8
00:00:58.394 --> 00:01:04.144
Riding horses in the heat makes you really thirsty. Trust me, I know!"

9
00:01:04.145 --> 00:01:09.071
Henry nodded. They were at the stable where Maggie took riding lessons.

10
00:01:09.072 --> 00:01:15.007
Today the stable was putting on a horse show for its students to show off what they'd been learning all summer.

11
00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:21.316
The stable's owner, Ms. Wood, had told Maggie that she and her friends could sell lemonade during the show.

12
00:01:21.317 --> 00:01:26.051
A rider hurried over. "Is the stand open yet?" she asked.

13
00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.245
"I'll take a lemonade, please."

14
00:01:28.246 --> 00:01:31.900
"Coming right up." Henry poured the girl a cup of lemonade.

15
00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:35.805
As he handed it to her, several more riders came over.

16
00:01:35.806 --> 00:01:41.282
For the next few minutes Henry and Maggie stayed busy serving lemonade to customers.

17
00:01:41.283 --> 00:01:45.935
"Where's Cole?" Maggie asked as she dropped a quarter into the cashbox.

18
00:01:45.936 --> 00:01:47.975
"We could use his help."

19
00:01:47.976 --> 00:01:52.350
"I think he went to look for more napkins," Henry said.

20
00:01:52.351 --> 00:01:56.942
"I'm not sure why, though. We already have plenty of them."

21
00:01:56.943 --> 00:01:58.953
A few girls hurried over.

22
00:01:58.954 --> 00:02:02.886
One of them was Daisy, who also rode at Maggie's stable.

23
00:02:02.887 --> 00:02:08.123
"One lemonade, please," a girl said. "I hope it's nice and cold!"

24
00:02:08.124 --> 00:02:11.665
"It is," Maggie said as she poured the girl a cup.

25
00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:15.357
The girl drank her lemonade quickly and left.

26
00:02:15.358 --> 00:02:21.495
"Some of these riders would be cooler if they took off their long-sleeved jackets," Henry said.

27
00:02:21.496 --> 00:02:24.895
"Those are show coats," Daisy said.

28
00:02:24.896 --> 00:02:28.629
"That's what you're supposed to wear for horse shows."

29
00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:33.876
"Oh. How come you and Maggie aren't wearing them?" Henry asked.

30
00:02:33.877 --> 00:02:39.179
Maggie frowned. "I wish I had a show coat to wear," she said.

31
00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.031
"But my mom and dad wouldn't buy me one.

32
00:02:42.032 --> 00:02:45.105
And I definitely can't afford to buy one myself.

33
00:02:45.106 --> 00:02:49.778
I barely had enough money to enter two classes in the show!"

34
00:02:49.779 --> 00:02:53.062
"Don't worry, Maggie," Daisy said.

35
00:02:53.063 --> 00:02:57.772
"Ms. Wood said you don't need fancy show clothes, remember?

36
00:02:57.773 --> 00:03:02.133
This show is supposed to be for learning and having fun."

37
00:03:02.134 --> 00:03:04.640
Henry looked at Daisy's T-shirt.

38
00:03:04.641 --> 00:03:09.179
"Are you wearing that bright pink T-shirt in the show?" he asked.

39
00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.013
Daisy shook her head.

40
00:03:11.014 --> 00:03:15.772
"I'm just wearing it in case I get dirty while I get my pony ready.

41
00:03:15.773 --> 00:03:19.555
My new show clothes are hanging by her stall."

42
00:03:19.556 --> 00:03:23.819
"Oh." Henry shrugged. He didn't know much about horseback riding.

43
00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:28.143
"Well, enjoy your lemonade." He handed Daisy a cup.

44
00:03:28.144 --> 00:03:32.296
"Thanks." Daisy took a sip, and then walked off.

45
00:03:32.297 --> 00:03:35.053
A moment later Cole rushed over.

46
00:03:35.054 --> 00:03:38.511
His face was sweaty and he was breathing hard.

47
00:03:38.512 --> 00:03:41.722
"Where are the napkins?" Henry asked him.

48
00:03:41.723 --> 00:03:45.116
"Huh?" Cole looked down at his empty hands.

49
00:03:45.117 --> 00:03:49.365
"Oh. I couldn't find any." He shrugged and glanced at the table.

50
00:03:49.366 --> 00:03:52.382
"Anyway, it looks like we have enough of them."

51
00:03:52.383 --> 00:03:54.016
Maggie frowned.

52
00:03:54.017 --> 00:03:58.040
"We've been busy, and you missed all the work," she complained.

53
00:03:58.041 --> 00:04:01.667
"Not all of it." Cole pointed toward some people.

54
00:04:01.668 --> 00:04:05.091
"Here come more customers."

55
00:04:05.092 --> 00:04:09.389
Henry and his friends served several thirsty riders and a few parents.

56
00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.902
Then Maggie checked her watch.

57
00:04:11.903 --> 00:04:15.939
"I need to get ready for my first class in the show," she said.

58
00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.201
"You guys will be okay without me for a while, right?"

59
00:04:19.202 --> 00:04:22.163
"Sure. Good luck," Henry said.

60
00:04:22.164 --> 00:04:27.992
After she left, a few more customers wandered over.

61
00:04:27.993 --> 00:04:31.580
Then several minutes passed without any customers at all.

62
00:04:31.581 --> 00:04:36.398
"Are you sure you don't want to go to your swim practice?" Henry asked Cole.

63
00:04:36.399 --> 00:04:40.927
"Maggie and I can probably handle the lemonade stand by ourselves."

64
00:04:40.928 --> 00:04:43.668
"No, that's okay," Cole said.

65
00:04:43.669 --> 00:04:48.244
"The coach said today's practice is mainly for the divers on the team."

66
00:04:48.245 --> 00:04:52.573
He pulled two bright green lollipops out of his pocket. "Want one?"

67
00:04:52.574 --> 00:04:56.385
"Sure, thanks!" Henry took one of the lollipops.

68
00:04:56.386 --> 00:05:00.041
"Aren't these the homemade ones from the Dessert Den?"

69
00:05:00.042 --> 00:05:03.885
"Yeah. I bought them when we went there yesterday," Cole said.

70
00:05:03.886 --> 00:05:07.039
"They're kiwi-flavored—my favorite!"

71
00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.317
Henry unwrapped his lollipop.

72
00:05:09.318 --> 00:05:12.497
It was sticky and partly melted because of the heat.

73
00:05:12.498 --> 00:05:14.755
But it still tasted good.

74
00:05:14.756 --> 00:05:18.683
After a moment he noticed that Cole's tongue was turning bright green.

75
00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:23.670
"Is my tongue green too?" Henry asked, sticking out his tongue.

76
00:05:23.671 --> 00:05:27.461
Cole grinned. "Yeah. You look like a zombie."

77
00:05:27.462 --> 00:05:32.274
"Too bad you don't have any cherry-flavored lollipops," Henry joked.

78
00:05:32.275 --> 00:05:35.422
"Then we could dye our tongues back to red."

79
00:05:35.423 --> 00:05:39.468
Before Cole could answer, Daisy raced up to the lemonade stand.

80
00:05:39.469 --> 00:05:41.750
Maggie was right behind her.

81
00:05:41.751 --> 00:05:45.936
"I need The Lemonade Detectives!" Daisy blurted out.

82
00:05:45.937 --> 00:05:52.109
"Someone stole my brand-new show shirt!"
